<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Generated samples from the pre-trained model and different unlearned models. (a), (c), (e), (g), (i), and (k) are generated using the pre-trained model while (b), (d), (f), (h), (j) and (l) are generated using the same noise vector from the corresponding unlearned models. The latter images on the LAION-5B dataset show the performance of <span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VDU</span> in unlearning ‘Van Gogh’ style from a Stable Diffusion model. More results can be found in Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.2.5 Feature Unlearned Samples using VDU ‣ A.2 Additional Results ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices and Supplementary Material ‣ Variational Diffusion Unlearning: A Variational Inference Framework for Unlearning in Diffusion Models under Data Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ A.2.4 Class Unlearned Samples using VDU ‣ A.2 Additional Results ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices and Supplementary Material ‣ Variational Diffusion Unlearning: A Variational Inference Framework for Unlearning in Diffusion Models under Data Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
